  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.50",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Does every finite 3-group $T$ have a nontrivial characteristic subgroup $C$ such that if $T$ is a Sylow 3-subgroup of a finite group $G$, then $T\\cap G'=T\\cap H'$, where $H=N_G(C)$?\n\nThe group $S_4$ shows that no such characteristic subgroups can be found in some Sylow 2-subgroups.",
